--TEST--
An isolate's argument is its own and is not ambient: two children spawned with different values disagree, a grandchild spawned with no `args:` reads `null` while its parent still reads what it was given, and a second read answers the same value — ADR 0012 § 6, ADR 0006 § *Decision*
--FILE nvs.toml--
# ADR 0118 § 2: `spawn script` goes through a door that asks for
# `script.spawn` first, and deny-by-default means a case with no
# configuration cannot spawn at all. It is granted for the whole tree, which
# is what lets the child below spawn a child of its own.
[capabilities.script]
spawn = true
--FILE inner.nvs--
<?nvs
// A grandchild. Nothing was passed to it, and nothing is inherited from the
// isolate that spawned it — the argument is a value that crossed once, not an
// ambient fact a whole tree of scripts can read.
echo "  inner: ", Core\Script::args() == null ? "null" : "a value", "\n";
--FILE outer.nvs--
<?nvs
// Read twice, before and after spawning a child of its own: the slot is the
// isolate's ownership root and a read borrows from it, so the second answer is
// the first one and the grandchild's spawn does not disturb it.
echo "  outer: ", Core\Script::args() as string, "\n";

var $grand = spawn script "inner.nvs" with(output: "capture");
echo (await $grand)->output;

echo "  outer again: ", Core\Script::args() as string, "\n";
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Two children, spawned from the same statement in the same parent, differing
// only in the value written at `args:`. A `Core\Script::args()` that read
// anything ambient would answer the same thing for both.
var $left = spawn script "outer.nvs" with(args: "left", output: "capture");
var $right = spawn script "outer.nvs" with(args: "right", output: "capture");

echo "left\n";
echo (await $left)->output;
echo "right\n";
echo (await $right)->output;

// And handing a value out does not put one on the giver: `args:` transfers
// into the child's arena, and this root — which nothing spawned — still reads
// the absence it started with, after two spawns and two awaits.
echo "parent: ", Core\Script::args() == null ? "null" : "a value", "\n";
--EXPECT--
left
  outer: left
  inner: null
  outer again: left
right
  outer: right
  inner: null
  outer again: right
parent: null
